tags: hibernated-disk

A limit of the node: the most disk that the hibernated instances of one parent that cannot pay hold together.

The value is an integer in bytes. Example: 21474836480. Above the limit, the node stops the oldest hibernated instances that cannot pay, and deletes their state.

The limit has no scope.

An absent limit is not a promise of no limit. The node is bound.

=== formal
class=limit
name=hibernated-disk
per=one parent: the client or the instance that started the instances
rule=Above the limit, the node stops the oldest hibernated instances that cannot pay, and deletes their state.
scope=none
unit=bytes
